WEBVTT

00:02:58.271 --> 00:03:01.128
Society in Britain came to have two levels:

00:03:01.128 --> 00:03:03.341
French-speaking aristocracy

00:03:03.341 --> 00:03:05.744
and Old English-speaking peasants.

00:03:05.744 --> 00:03:09.080
The French also brought many Roman Catholic clergymen with them

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.320
who added Latin words to the mix.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.234
Old English adapted and grew

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:15.788
as thousands of words flowed in,

00:03:15.788 --> 00:03:19.240
many having to do with government, law, and aristocracy.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.227
Words like council,

00:03:20.227 --> 00:03:20.823
marriage,

00:03:20.823 --> 00:03:21.708
sovereign,

00:03:21.708 --> 00:03:22.633
govern,

00:03:22.633 --> 00:03:23.367
damage,

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:24.995
and parliament.

00:03:25.117 --> 00:03:26.447
As the language expanded,

00:03:26.447 --> 00:03:28.433
English speakers quickly realized what to do

00:03:28.433 --> 00:03:31.117
if they wanted to sound sophisticated: